WEBVTT

00:17.183 --> 00:23.523
Now, all the surviving players
will be given a choice.

00:24.024 --> 00:27.986
Please select whether you will accept
permanent residence in this land

00:28.069 --> 00:30.280
or if you will not accept it.

00:36.828 --> 00:37.829
I…

00:41.291 --> 00:43.168
don't want permanent residence.

00:45.128 --> 00:46.129
I also…

00:50.091 --> 00:51.176
don't want it.

00:52.969 --> 00:57.599
PERMANENT RESIDENCE IN THIS LAND
ACCEPT / DO NOT ACCEPT

01:02.604 --> 01:04.689
Of course, I'll take it.

01:05.940 --> 01:07.734
I will gladly take it as well.

01:10.987 --> 01:15.158
This place offers endless possibilities.

01:33.134 --> 01:35.095
I saw a red light.

01:38.139 --> 01:39.140
But…

01:41.267 --> 01:45.480
I thought it was fireworks,
so I didn't pay much attention to it.

01:47.315 --> 01:51.152
I hid in a toilet stall with my friends.

01:53.655 --> 01:56.241
I won't go into how we got there.

01:59.035 --> 02:02.831
But then everything went quiet.

02:06.668 --> 02:09.796
I don't remember anything after that.

02:13.091 --> 02:17.178
The meteorite strike caused you
to go into cardiac arrest, correct?

02:18.638 --> 02:19.639
That's right.

02:20.890 --> 02:24.394
Do you remember anything else?

02:32.235 --> 02:33.486
There's nothing else.

02:36.781 --> 02:41.161
Do you remember dreaming
while you were unconscious?

02:42.829 --> 02:43.746
Did I dream?

02:45.748 --> 02:46.875
About games.

02:49.169 --> 02:50.086
"Games"?

02:50.712 --> 02:51.880
Did you?

02:52.714 --> 02:56.342
A dream about games
where your life was on the line.

03:07.437 --> 03:08.479
No.

03:11.149 --> 03:12.150
You didn't?

03:14.694 --> 03:15.528
But…

03:17.113 --> 03:18.031
But what?

03:21.326 --> 03:24.037
I feel like I dreamed about a journey.

03:25.955 --> 03:26.915
"A journey"?

03:29.292 --> 03:33.796
Like I went to… a far-off land.

03:44.557 --> 03:48.770
Don't push yourself too hard.
Thank you for your time today.

03:49.896 --> 03:54.275
Please, Matsuyama. No leading questions.

03:54.776 --> 03:58.238
They might distort his memories.

03:58.821 --> 04:01.282
Multiple survivors mentioned games.

04:01.366 --> 04:03.201
You may have planted the idea.

04:03.284 --> 04:07.664
Fireworks came up again.
Multiple survivors mentioned that.

04:07.747 --> 04:09.666
It was probably just the meteor.

04:11.542 --> 04:14.712
They all clearly experienced
the same thing.

04:25.181 --> 04:29.769
A former genius researching the afterlife…
He's lost it.

04:31.020 --> 04:32.939
He wasn't always like this.

04:33.022 --> 04:36.109
- The Shibuya meteorite changed everyone.
- No, before that.

04:36.609 --> 04:40.196
That accident five years ago,
where the student died.

04:40.905 --> 04:41.864
Oh, right.

04:42.865 --> 04:43.866
That.

04:49.080 --> 04:51.291
There was nothing I could do.

04:53.876 --> 04:55.003
I'm sorry.

04:58.339 --> 04:59.632
Forgive me.

05:31.539 --> 05:33.875
The main hall is that way. Thank you.

05:33.958 --> 05:35.251
You're welcome.

05:35.335 --> 05:36.377
Thank you.

05:40.131 --> 05:43.384
I found your dream
about a journey very interesting.

05:44.427 --> 05:46.387
I'd love to hear more sometime.

05:47.013 --> 05:50.016
Please contact me directly
if you remember anything.

05:50.099 --> 05:51.267
Okay, I will.

05:53.061 --> 05:55.396
Even if it seems absurd.

05:56.647 --> 05:57.648
"Absurd"?

05:58.441 --> 06:01.194
Something no one else would believe.

06:02.779 --> 06:03.654
All right?

06:09.369 --> 06:10.578
This way.

06:18.711 --> 06:19.545
Arisu.

06:20.963 --> 06:22.590
Hey. Sorry it took so long.

06:24.634 --> 06:27.095
- You must be tired.
- Sorry. Were you waiting long?

06:35.728 --> 06:37.021
This is my wife.

06:39.357 --> 06:42.235
- Mr. Matsuyama is an assistant professor.
- Hello.

06:43.152 --> 06:45.530
My wife was also interviewed here today.

06:46.656 --> 06:48.074
You were in Shibuya too?

06:48.574 --> 06:50.368
- That's right.
- I see.

06:52.036 --> 06:54.664
Would you tell me your story next time?

06:56.624 --> 06:59.419
- Okay.
- I'm Ryuji Matsuyama.

07:02.422 --> 07:05.550
ASST. PROFESSOR, DEPT. OF PSYCHOPATHOLOGY
SHUSHIKAN UNIVERSITY

07:05.633 --> 07:07.427
I'll be in touch.

07:09.679 --> 07:10.513
Sure.

07:18.146 --> 07:19.689
What did they ask you?

07:20.523 --> 07:23.234
A bunch of stuff
about dreams and other things.

07:25.027 --> 07:26.779
Like we could ever remember.

07:31.284 --> 07:34.412
I wish my university was this big.

07:35.746 --> 07:38.332
Have you gotten used to
your counseling internship?

07:38.916 --> 07:40.209
Yeah, pretty much.

07:41.002 --> 07:44.380
I bet I'll get hired full-time
after I graduate next year.

07:44.881 --> 07:48.593
Wow! I finally get a proper husband.

07:49.093 --> 07:49.927
Excuse me?

07:58.686 --> 07:59.812
Takuma Hagio.

08:01.564 --> 08:02.815
Sumiko Murakoshi.

08:02.899 --> 08:04.358
NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCES

08:04.442 --> 08:05.568
Saaya Ishii.

08:05.651 --> 08:07.862
ANSWERS FROM THE AFTERLIFE

08:07.945 --> 08:08.946
Shuto Aida.

08:11.157 --> 08:15.203
In my study,
the aforementioned ten subjects…

08:17.079 --> 08:19.040
spoke of near-death experiences.

08:20.583 --> 08:22.251
They all had…

08:22.335 --> 08:24.295
COHORT STUDY ON TOKYO METEORITE SURVIVORS

08:24.378 --> 08:26.297
…the exact same dream.

08:28.257 --> 08:29.258
A journey.

08:30.593 --> 08:31.719
A deserted city.

08:33.137 --> 08:34.096
Games.

08:35.765 --> 08:36.724
Fireworks.

08:42.605 --> 08:44.315
MESSAGE

08:47.818 --> 08:51.239
I CAN SEE YOUR AFTERLIFE

08:52.198 --> 08:53.616
FROM: NEAR-DEATH SUPPORT GROUP INFO

08:53.699 --> 08:55.785
THERE'S A SHADY GROUP USING GROUP HYPNOSIS

08:55.868 --> 08:57.245
TELL ME MORE. I'LL PAY 100 COINS

08:57.328 --> 08:58.663
DEAL. ASK "HIM" FOR DETAILS

08:58.746 --> 09:00.122
MR. LORD
VIEW PROFILE

09:00.206 --> 09:02.208
100 COINS
COINS SENT

09:03.543 --> 09:08.214
MR. R, I FOUND A LEAD
THAT MAY INTEREST YOU

09:35.283 --> 09:36.617
Whoa!

09:37.451 --> 09:39.787
I can't believe this is Shibuya.

09:39.870 --> 09:40.871
Seriously?

09:41.372 --> 09:42.456
Whoa!

10:51.942 --> 10:53.861
Are you Mr. R?

10:56.989 --> 10:59.158
Yes, I'm R.

11:11.671 --> 11:17.885
So… are you interested
in that seminar too?

11:20.012 --> 11:21.013
Yes.

11:21.722 --> 11:23.224
Could you invite me?

11:23.933 --> 11:26.143
I heard there's a strict referral…

11:27.895 --> 11:29.814
Let me know when you're ready.

11:30.981 --> 11:32.942
- Tea, please.
- I'll have the same.

11:34.026 --> 11:34.860
Okay.

11:37.988 --> 11:41.158
I wouldn't recommend it.

11:43.077 --> 11:43.911
But

11:45.329 --> 11:47.164
if you do go, you'll understand

11:48.124 --> 11:49.417
it's the real deal.

11:52.503 --> 11:54.755
What sort of experience did you have?

11:58.300 --> 12:00.261
We do strange things.

12:02.513 --> 12:05.474
"Strange things"? Like what?

12:09.812 --> 12:10.771
Games.

12:15.067 --> 12:15.985
"Games"?

12:17.695 --> 12:18.738
Yes.

12:19.739 --> 12:21.490
They're exhilarating.

12:23.242 --> 12:25.494
Like a sacred ritual.

12:39.467 --> 12:42.344
You'll receive an email invitation
in a week.

12:43.971 --> 12:46.724
Go to the specified location.

12:51.645 --> 12:53.022
INBOX: (NO SUBJECT)

13:17.588 --> 13:19.423
MR. R, THANK YOU FOR YOUR INTEREST

13:19.507 --> 13:22.968
AFTER CAREFUL REVIEW,
WE HEREBY INVITE YOU TO THE "SEMINAR"

13:28.516 --> 13:31.227
TUE, OCT 14, 2024, 23:00
KOTO SIDE OFFICE

13:31.310 --> 13:34.647
WE LOOK FORWARD
TO YOUR ATTENDANCE, MR. R

15:31.555 --> 15:34.016
Thank you for coming.

15:34.892 --> 15:37.186
Please be seated over here.

15:58.874 --> 16:00.292
Please take a seat.

16:02.044 --> 16:03.087
On that chair.

16:04.964 --> 16:07.341
You shouldn't move once you've sat down.

16:32.908 --> 16:35.995
Now then, let's begin the game.

16:37.538 --> 16:38.539
What game?

16:39.957 --> 16:43.043
I came here for a near-death experience.

16:43.752 --> 16:47.381
You can only take part in the journey
if you win this game.

16:49.008 --> 16:49.967
"Journey"?

16:54.179 --> 16:55.431
Let's begin.

16:56.682 --> 16:58.726
The game is Old Maid.

17:07.067 --> 17:08.485
Please take your cards.

17:17.161 --> 17:21.665
Any pairs in your hand must be discarded.

17:22.332 --> 17:23.292
I have a pair!

17:24.043 --> 17:28.630
Whoever has the Joker,
aka Old Maid, at the end wins.

17:30.632 --> 17:32.801
Okay, let's start with you.

17:34.595 --> 17:39.641
Note that whoever has the Joker
drawn from their hand is eliminated.

17:41.310 --> 17:42.144
What?

17:50.194 --> 17:51.737
You all heard me, right?

17:52.863 --> 17:55.365
You shouldn't move once you've sat down.

17:56.909 --> 18:00.120
If you do, you're eliminated.

18:02.456 --> 18:03.457
She's dead.

18:05.751 --> 18:08.337
No way. It's just an act, right?

19:31.128 --> 19:33.005
Now it's getting interesting.

20:07.789 --> 20:08.707
Crap.

20:27.226 --> 20:28.977
The odds are fifty-fifty.

20:29.561 --> 20:30.687
One of us will die.

21:42.301 --> 21:45.304
Welcome to Borderland.

23:36.581 --> 23:37.582
Dad?

24:18.540 --> 24:19.458
Are you okay?

24:21.001 --> 24:21.918
Yeah.

24:27.424 --> 24:28.717
Had a bad dream?

24:31.178 --> 24:32.262
Are you all right?

24:34.181 --> 24:36.266
Yeah, I'm fine.

24:39.394 --> 24:40.812
I just need some water.

24:50.113 --> 24:54.409
YUZUHA ARISU

24:54.493 --> 24:55.994
RESIDENTIAL LEASE

24:56.077 --> 24:59.873
We should consider buying someday
instead of renting, right?

25:00.415 --> 25:02.834
But first, we need to save some money.

25:03.919 --> 25:04.961
Right.

25:05.921 --> 25:08.256
We splurged on our wedding rings.

25:09.758 --> 25:10.634
True.

25:13.637 --> 25:15.222
What an unusual color.

25:15.305 --> 25:17.807
That? I bought it by accident.

25:18.600 --> 25:20.810
I really like this color.

25:20.894 --> 25:22.229
You can have it.

25:22.312 --> 25:23.396
Really? Yay.

25:25.482 --> 25:26.816
Want some help moving?

25:27.359 --> 25:30.237
No, I'll hire someone. I've got work too.

25:30.904 --> 25:32.781
I'll let you handle this.

25:32.864 --> 25:33.782
Sure.

25:34.449 --> 25:36.284
Gotta go. Bye.

25:36.868 --> 25:38.745
- Take care.
- See you.

25:42.582 --> 25:44.709
You're still brushing your teeth?

25:45.377 --> 25:46.962
You'll be late. Bye.

25:47.045 --> 25:48.129
Okay, see you.

25:56.096 --> 25:59.432
On the 19th of this month,
seven seminar attendees

25:59.516 --> 26:03.186
were found dead in a unit
of a mixed-use building

26:03.270 --> 26:04.771
in Koto City, Tokyo.

26:05.355 --> 26:10.443
Police are investigating the incident
as a possible group suicide.

26:13.488 --> 26:17.534
The Tokyo Bay Area
is popular with foreign tourists,

26:17.617 --> 26:20.996
and we expect
that they'll also visit our store.

26:21.079 --> 26:23.582
Then we should offer
a wide range of sizes.

26:23.665 --> 26:27.419
Like in Shibuya and Shinjuku,
where large sizes sell well.

26:27.502 --> 26:29.546
Right. I see your point.

26:34.134 --> 26:35.552
Here's the referral.

26:36.219 --> 26:39.306
This client was a victim
of the disaster at Shibuya Station.

26:40.765 --> 26:45.353
They have chronic PTSD
and are still suffering from flashbacks.

26:46.229 --> 26:48.106
Trauma from the meteorite incident.

26:49.524 --> 26:51.860
- Show them to the room.
- Will do.

26:53.987 --> 26:57.699
Excuse me. Would you please
fill out this medical questionnaire?

26:58.325 --> 27:00.619
Please include your name and address.

27:02.954 --> 27:05.540
Good morning.
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

27:08.793 --> 27:09.794
Please follow me.

27:25.018 --> 27:26.853
Can I get you something?

27:27.354 --> 27:29.981
We have coffee, tea… Whatever you like.

27:31.191 --> 27:32.484
Cold drinks too.

27:32.984 --> 27:33.985
Arisu.

27:39.074 --> 27:43.161
We've… met before.

27:45.830 --> 27:46.665
What?

28:39.217 --> 28:40.468
Our paths crossed

28:41.636 --> 28:43.722
in a far-off place.

28:46.182 --> 28:47.475
"A far-off place"?

28:49.102 --> 28:51.438
Some who had that near-death experience

28:52.814 --> 28:55.400
said they entered another world.

28:57.360 --> 28:59.446
Did they find hope there?

29:00.530 --> 29:03.074
Or did they find despair?

29:06.536 --> 29:10.498
You must have had
a near-death experience too.

29:12.792 --> 29:15.003
You should have memories of that world.

29:20.049 --> 29:21.050
Arisu…

29:22.510 --> 29:25.680
It's all real. You just don't remember it.

29:59.172 --> 30:03.468
You probably think I'm crazy.

30:04.677 --> 30:07.639
But that world is real.

30:09.140 --> 30:11.309
Both you and I

30:12.435 --> 30:14.479
fought there and survived.

30:17.065 --> 30:18.274
That's how we…

30:20.276 --> 30:21.986
returned to this world alive.

31:27.135 --> 31:31.264
I want to know what happened to us.

31:31.848 --> 31:34.267
So I did everything I could

31:35.310 --> 31:37.478
to find a way to return to that world.

31:39.856 --> 31:40.982
And I found one.

31:42.317 --> 31:44.861
A way to enter that world…

31:49.032 --> 31:50.742
by using a certain drug.

31:53.620 --> 31:54.913
Sorry for the wait.

31:57.123 --> 31:58.499
Please have a seat.

32:49.842 --> 32:51.886
INCOMING CALL
YUZUHA USAGI

32:54.055 --> 32:55.181
Quitting time?

32:56.182 --> 32:57.183
Arisu…

32:57.934 --> 32:59.143
Wanna come over?

33:04.023 --> 33:05.191
What's wrong?

33:06.359 --> 33:07.318
Where are you?

33:09.529 --> 33:10.530
Arisu…

33:12.407 --> 33:13.241
Yeah?

33:14.575 --> 33:15.660
I'll come get you.

33:24.002 --> 33:24.919
Usagi?

33:27.672 --> 33:28.631
I'm sorry.

33:30.133 --> 33:31.134
Usagi?

33:43.021 --> 33:45.940
The person you are trying
to reach is unavailable.

34:14.844 --> 34:15.803
Usagi?

34:21.559 --> 34:22.393
You there?

34:25.188 --> 34:29.400
The Public Safety Division
is also investigating this.

34:30.068 --> 34:33.905
At this point,
nothing suspicious has been found.

34:34.489 --> 34:37.742
But she still hasn't even
contacted her workplace.

34:37.825 --> 34:41.621
There is something
we'd like you to look at.

34:41.704 --> 34:42.622
Show him.

34:45.041 --> 34:49.212
This is security footage from the hotel
where your wife was last seen.

34:51.130 --> 34:54.425
It's a resort hotel in the Tokyo Bay Area.

34:58.971 --> 35:00.932
Do you recognize this man?

35:04.102 --> 35:04.936
Yes.

35:05.937 --> 35:07.355
I met him once before.

35:08.481 --> 35:10.608
He teaches at Shushikan University.

35:11.109 --> 35:13.152
Was he acquainted with your wife?

35:14.487 --> 35:17.865
We met him at his school
about two weeks ago.

35:22.495 --> 35:24.205
Did he abduct her?

35:25.665 --> 35:28.751
No, there's a more plausible explanation.

35:30.044 --> 35:31.879
I hate to say this,

35:32.380 --> 35:37.343
but could she have been
secretly meeting with him?

35:38.886 --> 35:40.638
It is a hotel, after all.

35:40.721 --> 35:42.932
And since you say they're acquainted,

35:43.432 --> 35:48.396
you might want to look into this
before filing a missing person report.

35:58.239 --> 36:01.033
I can't find my wife.

36:01.117 --> 36:03.744
She met with the professor
before I lost contact.

36:04.829 --> 36:08.916
Professor Matsuyama hasn't been
answering his phone either.

36:09.000 --> 36:10.001
What?

36:16.090 --> 36:20.970
He was obsessed
with strange subjects like the afterlife.

36:21.512 --> 36:24.473
But it's not like him
to be absent without notice,

36:24.557 --> 36:26.767
so we wondered if something happened.

36:34.650 --> 36:38.905
He was also investigating occult meetings.

36:39.739 --> 36:40.573
It was scary.

36:40.656 --> 36:42.116
MASS SUICIDES AND CULTS

36:42.200 --> 36:43.326
NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCES

36:43.409 --> 36:45.578
Was your wife involved too?

36:56.631 --> 37:00.343
DID SHIGENORI USAGI KILL HIMSELF
AFTER STAGED-CLIMB ACCUSATIONS?

37:03.930 --> 37:06.140
YUZUHA ARISU

37:12.605 --> 37:16.108
YUZUHA ARISU: INTERVIEW

37:16.192 --> 37:18.819
Do you dream often?

37:22.240 --> 37:23.783
I think so.

37:25.993 --> 37:27.453
What sort of dreams?

37:28.037 --> 37:29.956
Could you be more specific?

37:36.921 --> 37:39.548
I see the same scene over and over.

37:41.634 --> 37:42.760
Is it

37:44.053 --> 37:45.054
a nightmare?

37:49.141 --> 37:50.142
My father…

37:54.897 --> 37:56.315
He kills himself.

37:59.443 --> 38:00.319
I see.

38:03.030 --> 38:04.699
Any issues with him?

38:05.866 --> 38:07.034
None at all.

38:09.453 --> 38:11.330
My dad was a wonderful person.

38:13.874 --> 38:15.001
Could it be that

38:16.502 --> 38:18.796
you didn't get to say goodbye?

38:20.214 --> 38:22.049
Or that you have regrets?

38:29.056 --> 38:30.266
Don't push yourself.

38:33.853 --> 38:35.146
No, please listen.

38:36.856 --> 38:39.066
I can't tell anyone else.

38:40.943 --> 38:42.153
Even your husband?

38:45.197 --> 38:48.534
I don't… want to tell him.

38:52.288 --> 38:54.915
I met my husband, and we got married.

38:56.375 --> 38:58.753
I should be getting on with my life.

39:01.422 --> 39:03.632
But I'm still hung up on my dad.

39:14.060 --> 39:15.561
When I dream,

39:16.937 --> 39:20.858
I can feel my dad's presence.

39:22.193 --> 39:24.028
It's like he's right there.

39:26.864 --> 39:28.532
Even if I cry…

39:30.493 --> 39:31.660
Even if it hurts…

39:35.289 --> 39:36.957
Even if I see him kill himself…

39:38.084 --> 39:39.960
If my dad is there…

39:53.432 --> 39:55.226
Even if it's a nightmare…

39:58.020 --> 39:59.355
I want to be there.

40:20.459 --> 40:23.921
The player who played a part
in winning every single game…

40:25.172 --> 40:27.800
I became a citizen thanks to you.

40:36.016 --> 40:37.435
I've wanted to meet you.

40:38.894 --> 40:42.815
Won't you return to that beautiful world?

40:51.615 --> 40:53.659
It will all come back to you.

40:54.743 --> 40:57.079
Then you, too, will return to that world.

41:00.708 --> 41:01.959
Let the games begin.

41:07.673 --> 41:10.759
Your beloved will also be participating…

41:13.012 --> 41:14.013
in the games.

41:18.726 --> 41:19.685
Let's have fun.

42:00.267 --> 42:02.561
- How is she?
- She's in a coma.

42:02.645 --> 42:05.689
But she could go
into cardiac arrest at any moment.

42:05.773 --> 42:09.401
There were no signs of resistance
or a violent struggle.

42:09.485 --> 42:11.028
According to the doctor,

42:11.111 --> 42:15.574
the man she was with may have forced her
to take some kind of drug.

42:15.658 --> 42:16.784
A drug?

42:16.867 --> 42:18.452
It might be a murder-suicide.

42:20.246 --> 42:21.830
Doctor, he's here.

42:23.666 --> 42:25.709
- You're the husband?
- Yes.

42:26.585 --> 42:30.714
I know this is a bad time,
but according to a blood test,

42:31.966 --> 42:34.093
your wife is pregnant.

42:34.927 --> 42:35.803
What?

42:35.886 --> 42:39.473
It's still early,
so we can't detect a heartbeat.

42:39.974 --> 42:42.393
Your wife might not have known.

42:43.644 --> 42:44.562
You can go in.

43:10.713 --> 43:12.298
Usagi.

43:14.592 --> 43:17.678
This is the man
who was found collapsed with her.

43:18.887 --> 43:20.222
Please have a look.

43:32.610 --> 43:33.861
So you recognize him?

43:34.778 --> 43:37.406
Can we ask you some questions?

43:47.207 --> 43:52.838
Have you heard about
the mass suicides in Tokyo?

43:54.340 --> 43:55.341
What?

43:56.091 --> 43:59.386
Are you saying that guy abducted my wife

43:59.887 --> 44:02.514
and got her mixed up
in those mass suicides?

44:02.598 --> 44:06.602
It seems he'd been attending
those seminars.

44:06.685 --> 44:09.313
We traced their movements after the hotel.

44:10.397 --> 44:14.652
First, she was taken
to the university where he worked.

44:14.735 --> 44:19.531
After that, they went to the building
where they were found unconscious.

44:20.741 --> 44:25.496
Your wife may have gotten
mixed up in this case.

44:29.041 --> 44:30.668
I tried to tell you.

44:32.211 --> 44:34.963
But you wouldn't listen!

44:36.423 --> 44:42.721
We can't act without concrete evidence.

44:50.062 --> 44:51.146
May we ask you…

44:53.774 --> 44:56.443
to check your wife's belongings?

45:01.365 --> 45:06.995
If something seems out of place,
please let us know.

45:59.131 --> 45:59.965
Well?

46:02.259 --> 46:03.260
Notice anything?

46:04.011 --> 46:07.681
Your beloved will also be participating.

46:11.935 --> 46:13.270
No, nothing.

46:15.272 --> 46:16.899
That Joker card…

46:17.649 --> 46:20.819
Matsuyama had one too.

46:28.452 --> 46:30.579
Even if it seems absurd.

46:31.789 --> 46:33.081
"Absurd"?

46:33.165 --> 46:35.918
Something no one else would believe.

46:36.460 --> 46:38.003
"A far-off place"?

46:38.086 --> 46:40.088
That world is real.

46:48.889 --> 46:51.809
TAKINOGAWA SANATORIUM

46:59.817 --> 47:00.818
This way.

47:02.069 --> 47:03.737
The train will be stopping…

47:12.871 --> 47:15.999
My wife is in a coma.

47:17.459 --> 47:18.627
And she's pregnant.

47:19.920 --> 47:22.589
But her heart may soon stop.

47:23.382 --> 47:25.008
It's only a matter of time.

47:27.636 --> 47:31.306
A guy gave me this yesterday.

47:34.268 --> 47:36.395
You told me about that world.

47:37.187 --> 47:41.316
You said we fought there, survived,
and returned to this world.

47:43.235 --> 47:45.404
That guy said something similar.

47:47.406 --> 47:52.619
They might take my wife and child away
to that world.

47:55.455 --> 47:57.291
I know it sounds crazy.

47:58.667 --> 48:04.256
But I'd do anything
if there was a way to bring my wife back.

48:05.257 --> 48:06.258
Tell me.

48:14.933 --> 48:15.809
Two minutes.

48:16.935 --> 48:17.811
What?

48:20.063 --> 48:22.858
Once someone goes into cardiac arrest,

48:23.650 --> 48:28.280
they'll die if their heart doesn't
resume beating within two minutes.

48:28.947 --> 48:33.160
In the two minutes between cardiac arrest
and irreversible death,

48:34.578 --> 48:37.956
I believe people enter
a shared consciousness.

48:39.666 --> 48:42.085
That's the world we experienced.

48:42.169 --> 48:46.757
If you go there
and bring her back within two minutes…

48:48.842 --> 48:50.552
she might survive.

48:53.221 --> 48:54.473
"Within two minutes"?

48:56.350 --> 48:58.352
When we were there,

48:59.102 --> 49:00.812
it felt like a long time.

49:01.647 --> 49:08.153
But our hearts only stopped
for one minute.

49:09.363 --> 49:11.198
Time flows differently

49:11.698 --> 49:16.078
between the real world
and the shared consciousness.

49:17.537 --> 49:18.455
Two minutes.

49:19.373 --> 49:23.669
That moment in time
may feel like an eternity.

49:27.839 --> 49:29.508
Is that really possible?

49:30.425 --> 49:32.719
Isn't that why you're here?

49:37.015 --> 49:38.892
But I haven't tried it yet.

49:39.518 --> 49:43.397
There's no guarantee
you'll make it back alive.

49:43.480 --> 49:45.190
And if I don't make it back?

49:47.526 --> 49:49.027
You'll die, of course.

49:49.861 --> 49:54.491
And I'll be charged with
assisted suicide or murder.

50:07.129 --> 50:08.046
Yes?

50:10.757 --> 50:11.591
I see.

50:17.931 --> 50:19.433
Her heart stopped?

50:27.149 --> 50:28.483
I don't care if I die.

50:30.736 --> 50:32.779
If there's a chance I can save Usagi,

50:33.739 --> 50:34.906
I'll take it.

50:51.256 --> 50:53.759
INSULINACT

50:56.094 --> 50:57.220
That drug…

50:57.721 --> 50:59.473
It will stop your heart

51:00.182 --> 51:01.308
on purpose.

51:01.391 --> 51:02.517
Stop my heart?

51:03.060 --> 51:04.478
No time to think.

51:04.561 --> 51:05.479
Well?

51:13.987 --> 51:15.113
Two minutes.

51:16.156 --> 51:17.074
Right.

51:32.589 --> 51:33.924
Feel anything?

51:34.007 --> 51:35.258
Nothing.

51:38.637 --> 51:40.347
We're running out of time!

51:47.854 --> 51:48.855
The clock…

52:01.618 --> 52:02.536
Ann?

52:07.541 --> 52:08.542
Ann?

53:17.527 --> 53:20.947
PROCEED 15 KM SOUTH-SOUTHEAST
THE "GAME" STARTS AT SUNDOWN

54:19.965 --> 54:21.007
Usagi?

54:23.218 --> 54:30.225
THE "GAME" ARENA IS 6 KM AHEAD

54:51.371 --> 54:53.581
"GAME" ARENA AHEAD

56:32.263 --> 56:34.557
FRIED NOODLES

56:34.641 --> 56:36.101
COTTON CANDY

56:47.946 --> 56:51.741
Player quota reached.
Registration is now closed.

56:52.909 --> 56:56.955
A new team has been formed
at Hikawa Shrine.

57:07.757 --> 57:09.426
The game will now commence.

59:51.462 --> 59:55.133
Subtitle translation by: Jason Franzman
